{"n": 1300, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "1300.webp", "text": "0\n\nr2 09\"\n\n72-115\n\nChecking Automatic Seat Belts:\n\nThe automatic reel has two independent activat-\ning systems for the locking effect.\n\nThe first activating system should lock the reel\nwhen driving fast in curves, driving in tight\ncurves, when car rolls over, during sharp brak-\n‘ing or by impact,\n\nThis activation is accomplished with a ball (1).\nTo check, seat must be set upright and both\nhands placed on steering wheel in supporting\nPosition.\n\nThen apply brakes fully while driving at a road\nspeed equal to twice walking speed {road must\nbe dry).\n\nThe seat belt should lock.\n\nThe second activating system is for additional\nsafety and is controlled by inertia mass (2).\n\nIf reel locks when pulling out belt suddenly,\nthis system is also okay.\n\nThe belt should retract automatically as far as\npossible when released,\n\nIt could happen that the last section of the belt\nwill have to be guided to the door beam by hand.\nIf this last section is not wound, there could be\n@ weak or broken return spring (3) and/or exces-\nsive friction in the belt guides.\n\nAn unusuable seat belt or a seat belt worn ina\nserious accident should be destroyed immedi\nately after removal to guarantee that it cannot\nbe used again.\n\nThe automatic reel does not require servicing\n\nand must not be opened.\n\n72072099\n\n3072021\n\nThe automatic seat belt has to be replaced when\nthe mounting bar (6) is bent or the stirrup is dis-\ntorted in area (7).\n\nThe stirrup must still pivot after mounting bolt\nhas been tightened; only applicable to front\nseat belts,\n\nTo fasten a belt the tongue should insert easily\nand engage in the lock with a loud click.\n\nWhen pushing in the “PRESS” button the belt\ntongue will be ejected from the lock by spring\nforce.\n\nReplace seat belt when lock trim is missing or\ndamaged.\n\nWhen replacing a seat belt also replace the lower\nstrap,\n\nIn the case of belts integrated in seats an impact\ncould defform the lower strap stop on the seat\nrail.\n\nNever attempt to straighten the seat or seat rails.\n\nDeformed stirrups (1) must be replaced.\n\nIf the plastic cover in the opening for the belt\nabove the anchorage bar (16) has traces of\nwear, the seat belt must be replaced.", "words": [["0", 0.1996, 0.2772, 0.2118, 0.2838], ["r2", 0.2178, 0.2772, 0.2249, 0.2832], ["09\"", 0.2295, 0.2772, 0.2447, 0.2825], ["72-115", 0.4681, 0.0199, 0.5405, 0.0444], ["Checking", 0.2584, 0.0637, 0.3019, 0.0769], ["Automatic", 0.306, 0.0637, 0.3556, 0.0743], ["Seat", 0.3592, 0.0637, 0.3794, 0.0749], ["Belts:", 0.3835, 0.0637, 0.4098, 0.0749], ["The", 0.2584, 0.0955, 0.2766, 0.1061], ["automatic", 0.2791, 0.0955, 0.3278, 0.1068], ["reel", 0.3313, 0.0955, 0.3475, 0.1068], ["has", 0.3511, 0.0955, 0.3663, 0.1068], ["two", 0.3693, 0.0975, 0.3875, 0.1068], ["independent", 0.3911, 0.0955, 0.4493, 0.1088], ["activat-", 0.4529, 0.0975, 0.4873, 0.1068], ["ing", 0.2579, 0.1114, 0.2715, 0.1247], ["systems", 0.2751, 0.1134, 0.3126, 0.1247], ["for", 0.3156, 0.1114, 0.3298, 0.122], ["the", 0.3328, 0.1114, 0.348, 0.122], ["locking", 0.3516, 0.1114, 0.3855, 0.1247], ["effect.", 0.3886, 0.1114, 0.4184, 0.1227], ["The", 0.2579, 0.1273, 0.2756, 0.1379], ["first", 0.2796, 0.1273, 0.2984, 0.1379], ["activating", 0.3019, 0.1273, 0.348, 0.1412], ["system", 0.3511, 0.1293, 0.3835, 0.1406], ["should", 0.3865, 0.128, 0.4174, 0.1386], ["lock", 0.4215, 0.128, 0.4412, 0.1386], ["the", 0.4448, 0.1286, 0.46, 0.1386], ["reel", 0.4635, 0.1286, 0.4802, 0.1386], ["when", 0.2579, 0.1432, 0.2827, 0.1545], ["driving", 0.2867, 0.1432, 0.3197, 0.1565], ["fast", 0.3232, 0.1432, 0.3394, 0.1545], ["in", 0.3435, 0.1432, 0.3516, 0.1545], ["curves,", 0.3551, 0.1466, 0.387, 0.1565], ["driving", 0.3906, 0.1439, 0.4235, 0.1572], ["in", 0.4265, 0.1466, 0.4352, 0.1545], ["tight", 0.4387, 0.1439, 0.461, 0.1572], ["curves,", 0.2579, 0.1618, 0.2903, 0.1724], ["when", 0.2938, 0.1592, 0.3191, 0.1704], ["car